  "lineage": "Japanese 'paper-play' storytelling in which a narrator performs a tale by sliding illustrated cards through a small wooden proscenium (butai), reading the text printed on the back while showing the picture in front. Popularised by itinerant street performers in the 1920s-1950s who drew children with candy sales before the advent of television, and later adapted for classroom and library use, it is a documented Showa-era mass-entertainment form. Delivery is animated, dramatic spoken narration timed to the beat of each card-change, with distinct character voices and cliffhanger pacing.",
